+---
+id: dl-001-rental-periods-strict-utc-midnight-format-half-open-overlap-sequential-booking-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "Rental periods: strict UTC-midnight format, half-open overlap, sequential booking ids"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+The rental module must follow the school's rules: integer euro cents, UTC ISO-8601 times, whole-day
+periods ending at the start of the day after the last day, no overlapping bookings of one item.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A period is accepted only if `start` and `end` are strings of the form `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00[.000]Z`
+  and `end` is after `start`. Offsets, date-only strings and non-midnight times are rejected rather than
+  converted, so a desk typo is never silently re-priced.
+- Periods are half-open `[start, end)`: two bookings of one item conflict when `a.start < b.end` and
+  `b.start < a.end`; back-to-back bookings are allowed.
+- Total = number of days x `dailyPrice`; `dailyPrice` must be a non-negative safe integer of cents.
+- Booking ids are sequential (`booking-1`, ...) per service instance, to stay deterministic (no
+  randomness or wall clock).
+- Equipment ids are unique; adding a duplicate throws.
+- Cancellation (rule 5) is not implemented yet, as requested.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Callers must send canonical UTC-midnight strings. Ids are unique only within one service instance, which
+is enough for the in-memory store; a persistent store will need a new id scheme.
